{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Oil for illumination</b> — defective (without vav), for it is not needed for illumination. Thirteen things are enumerated here, and likewise there are thirteen types of garments in Ezekiel: ואנעלך תחש ('and I shod you with tahash') etc., and ואעדך עדי ('and I adorned you with jewelry') etc. And when Israel sinned with the calf they lost thirteen garments, as written: ויתנצלו בני ישראל את עדים ('and the children of Israel stripped themselves of their ornaments'). And by the merit of these thirteen types that they donated, the thirteen were restored to them:"], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The word שמן למאור (Exodus 25:6) is written defective without the vav in למאר; Ba'al HaTurim reads this as indicating the oil is not needed 'for illumination' (לאורה), likely referring to the anointing oil rather than the Menorah oil."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:20.066180453Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}